In the latest edition of "Who the fuck designed this encounter?", our intrepid heroes found themselves in the Plane of Innovation, squaring off against the evil machinations of the Manaetic Behemoth.  The plot line goes something like this: we engage, we kill the behemoth, stupid room traps kill us, people buy tickets to San Diego to kick the shit outa VI zone designers.  However with a little ingenuity we finally managed to get most people flagged and averted any homicidal rampages.
<br>
<br>
<center><img src="images/gnomeshiz.jpg"></center>
<br>
<br>
Lets see, what else have we been up to?  Ok time to unload more pent up flag-encounter hate.  The maze in PoN, you should get a damn flag just for managing to get 3 groups in the same maze.  I know they meant well by having the possibility to have 3 of those going in parallel, but at least have the quest mob say, "HEY, SOME OTHER MORONS WERE HERE 2 HOURS AGO AND LEFT THE THING ALL FUBAR, MMMKAY?".  On the plus side, the first time through that encounter was fun.  No comment on the 4th time through.
<br>
<br>
We've also been exploring VT some here and there.  VT looks great, awesome zone design, though you can't really appreciate how many mobs are in that zone until you spend a few days in there clearing.  Still a lot of fun.  Other than that, we've been doing some farming as well - Emp, Cursed, Seru, etc... nothing too notable, 'cept that Seru finally gave up the goods and dropped 2(!) BP's for us tonight.
